      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The primary risk you're mitigating is SMS interception, which is a major vulnerability. SMS is easily susceptible to SIM-swapping attacks, where a malicious actor convinces a mobile carrier to port your number to their control. Furthermore, SMS messages can be intercepted via SS7 network vulnerabilities, making them a weak link in your security chain. Hardware keys, using FIDO2/U2F standards, eliminate these risks because they rely on cryptographic challenges and physical possession, not easily intercepted signals.",
