      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When pitching to partners, you need to frame this in terms of evolving threats, not just \"hackers.\" You can describe the threat actors as ranging from opportunistic script-kiddies to highly organized, targeted adversaries. The difference is that a typical hacker might try to brute-force a password, but SIM-swapping and SMS interception are attacks executed by sophisticated actors who are specifically targeting the *human element* and the *telecom infrastructure*—a much more insidious threat.\n\nYou can tell them, \"We are moving from trusting a fragile, easily hijacked carrier signal to requiring verifiable, physical proof of identity.\" This sounds much more strategic than just saying \"we're blocking SMS.\" It highlights the shift from weak authentication to strong, phishing-resistant MFA.",
